# MQTT transport

This file defines the **MQTT protocol contract** for an Edge Agent process that
**owns a broker client**. It is not a broker product catalog.

**Ownership of the device-root cloud session** (agent vs host supervisor vs
other) is **product topology** — document in consumer ADRs. This constitution
does not require the agent to be the sole device MQTT gateway.

When the agent does **not** own device-root MQTT, uplink/downlink may arrive
via a host-local client seam; still apply plane doctrine
(**`two-plane-architecture.mdc`**) and reconciliation
(**`desired-state-reconciliation.mdc`**). Protocol defaults below apply to any
MQTT client the agent process does open.

## Client contract (constitution default)

| Concern | Default |
|---------|---------|
| Protocol | **MQTT v5** |
| QoS (telemetry + desired-state) | **QoS 1** |
| Session | **Persistent session** (survives reconnect; no lost retained intent) |
| Auth / transport security | **mTLS** client certificates |
| Desired-state delivery | **Retained** (or equivalent shadow) messages so intermittent devices always see latest intent |

Reference client libraries for the agent's own process: **`paho-mqtt`** /
**`aiomqtt`**. Broker **product** choice is a consumer foundation + ADR concern.

## Topic and ACL mechanics

- Prefer **per-device topic namespaces** with broker ACLs so one device cannot
  publish or subscribe as another.
- Topic **catalog strings** (exact names) live in consumer
  **`docs/specification/product/`** and settings — not hardcoded inventively
  across modules.
- Do **not** adopt QoS 2 without an ADR (**`edge-agent-adr.mdc`**). Prefer
  QoS 1 + **idempotent downstream keys** (e.g. inference / correlation ID).

## Uplink vs downlink jobs

- **Uplink:** publish telemetry from disk-backed buffers; never publish from
  RAM-only queues across power cycles (**`local-buffer-pattern.mdc`**).
- **Downlink:** subscribe to desired-state; reconcile when online
  (**`desired-state-reconciliation.mdc`**). MQTT's strength for intermittent
  devices is a primary justification for the broker — stronger than uplink alone.

## Anti-patterns

- Pushing model binaries through the broker
- Holding the only copy of desired-state in agent RAM without retained/cloud
  shadow backup
- Silent cleartext MQTT in any environment without an ADR with expiry
- Encoding product topic catalogs or campaign schemas in this package

